# Cfx.re / FiveM — Open-Source Docs & Code Index

Collected 2026-10-24 from the official docs site and the public GitHub API
(`api.github.com/orgs/citizenfx/repos` — 87 repos in the org). Everything below
is the official Cfx.re surface. "Open on GitHub" does **not** automatically mean
"free to reuse" — check each repo's license first (noted where GitHub reports one;
many repos report no license, which legally means all-rights-reserved by default).

## 1. The official documentation — docs.fivem.net
Source repo: https://github.com/citizenfx/fivem-docs (the site is built from it; PRs welcome)

| Section (in the repo) | What it covers | Why you need it |
|---|---|---|
| `getting-started` | Installing FiveM, setting up a server | Your Phase 0 — start here |
| `server-manual` | server.cfg, convars/commands, txAdmin setup, OneSync, proxy, server issues | Running FXServer legally and correctly |
| `client-manual` | Player client install/troubleshooting | Support docs for your players |
| `scripting-manual` | Lua/JS/C# resource scripting: events, exports, state bags, NUI | The core of your custom Lua resources |
| `scripting-reference` | Runtimes, fxmanifest reference, function/command reference | Lookup while coding |
| `resources` | Per-resource docs for the bundled/default resources | How chat, mapmanager, etc. behave |
| `developers` | Developer tooling and internals | Deeper platform work |
| `cookbook` | Short recipes/snippets for common tasks | Fast answers for small features |
| `game-references` | Vehicle/weapon/ped models, blips, etc. | IDs/hashes for jobs, vehicles, HUD |
| `fxdk` | FxDK (the in-world creator tool / editor) | Building/testing content in-game |
| `assets-manual` | Streaming custom assets (models, textures, audio) | Custom cars/maps later |
| `support` | Client/server troubleshooting | First stop when something breaks |
| `contributing` | How to contribute to the docs/code | If you PR fixes upstream |
| `alchemist` | Alchemist asset conversion tooling | Asset pipeline |

## 2. Natives reference (the GTA V function bible)
- Site: https://docs.fivem.net/natives/ — every native, searchable by namespace
- Source repo: https://github.com/citizenfx/natives — "GTA V Natives Documentation"
  (folders per namespace: PED, VEHICLE-adjacent namespaces like ENTITY, HUD, NETWORK, AUDIO, GRAPHICS…)
- Tooling: https://github.com/citizenfx/native-doc-tooling

## 3. Key open-source code repos (citizenfx org — the ones that matter for a server build)
| Repo | What it is | License (per GitHub) |
|---|---|---|
| citizenfx/fivem | Source for FiveM, RedM and FXServer itself (C++) | NOASSERTION — dual license, read `code/LICENSE` in-repo before any reuse |
| citizenfx/fivem-docs | Source of docs.fivem.net | none declared |
| citizenfx/natives | GTA V natives database powering the natives reference | none declared |
| citizenfx/cfx-server-data | The default/bundled server resources (chat, mapmanager, spawnmanager…) in `[gamemodes] [gameplay] [local] [managers] [system] [test]` | none declared |
| citizenfx/cfx-server-data-experimental | Experimental variants of the default resources | none declared |
| citizenfx/example-resources | Small example resources to learn resource structure from | none declared |
| citizenfx/txAdmin | Official server management panel (27k+ servers) — TypeScript | MIT |
| citizenfx/txAdmin-recipes | Official txAdmin deployer recipes (one-click server bases) | MIT |
| citizenfx/txAdmin-playerGen | Dev tool to mock txAdmin player lists | MIT |
| citizenfx/screenshot-basic | Client screenshot resource (TypeScript) | MIT |
| citizenfx/fxcode | FxDK code editor (VS Code fork) | MIT |
| citizenfx/AnimKit | Tool for creating/editing GTA V animations (C#) | AGPL-3.0 |
| citizenfx/cfx-dotnet | .NET runtime support for FXServer (C# resources) | none declared |
| citizenfx/msgpack-cs | C# MsgPack for FiveM/RedM/FXServer | none declared |
| citizenfx/lua | The Lua interpreter mirror FiveM ships (Lua 5.4 line) | none declared |
| citizenfx/lua-cmsgpack · lua-rapidjson · lmprof | Lua modules/profiler bundled for resources | mixed (rapidjson MIT; others none declared) |
| citizenfx/NativeUI | Classic GTA V UI/menu library (C#) | MIT |
| citizenfx/project-lambdamenu | Lambda Menu for CitizenFX | none declared |
| citizenfx/http-wrapper | HTTP wrapper for Node.js usage in CitizenFX | none declared |
| citizenfx/rfc | Community feedback / RFCs for Cfx products | none declared |

The other ~60 repos in the org are mostly upstream forks/libraries FiveM builds on
(Chromium/CEF, bgfx, imgui, enet, libuv, mono, node, EASTL, oneTBB, etc.) — useful
only if you are building FiveM itself, not a server on top of it.

